      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "| Feature | Exchange-Traded Funds (ETFs) | Mutual Funds |\n|---------|------------------------------|--------------|\n| Liquidity | High, as they trade like stocks on an exchange. | Lower, as they are bought and sold at the end of the trading day at the net asset value. |\n| Pricing | Fluctuates throughout the trading day, similar to a stock's price. | Fixed once per day at the end of the trading day, like a fixed price on a market stall. |\n| Management Style | Often passive, with a \"track the market\" approach, like a well-trained horde following a set path. | Can be either active or passive, like a diverse group of creatures, some following the path and others charting their own course. |\n\nETFs are like a well-organized band of goblins, each one following the same path, ensuring they all move together in harmony. Mutual Funds, on the other hand, are more like a group of goblins with different personalities, some sticking to the beaten path while others explore new trails.",
